From 20766a34807e3438be6d9f3dc2016d49b2c37277 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Certe Kim <18364439+CerteKim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:17:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8180x-xiaomi-book-12.4: attach to the
 DSPs in EL2

The ADSP, CDSP and SLPI are started and owned by the firmware. In EL2 the PAS
reset sequence is not available, so Linux can authenticate a firmware image but
the remoteproc never leaves reset:

  qcom_q6v5_pas 17300000.remoteproc: start timed out
  remoteproc remoteproc3: can't start rproc adsp: -110

Describe that as "qcom,broken-reset" (plus "qcom,needs-tzmem" for the SHM
bridge) and let the driver attach to whichever DSP the boot firmware left
running, instead of describing them as disabled and not using them at all.

Signed-off-by: Certe Kim <18364439+CerteKim@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-el2.dtso | 24 ++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-el2.dtso b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-el2.dtso
index 4bfea03..3cf565e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-el2.dtso
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-el2.dtso
@@ -36,12 +36,15 @@
  *    reporting for banks 107..126.  TODO: replace them with the real 21
  *    interrupts once the vendor's IORT/ACPI data is available.
  *
- *  - The ADSP, CDSP and SLPI are started and owned by the firmware.  In EL2
- *    Linux can neither authenticate their firmware (-EINVAL) nor reset them,
- *    and the remoteproc driver shuts the subsystems down after the failed
- *    start, which resets the machine.  Not describing them keeps the driver
- *    away.  qcom_q6v5_attach()-style support (attaching to the already
- *    running remoteprocs) is the long-term fix.
+ *  - The ADSP, CDSP and SLPI are started and owned by the firmware, and in
+ *    EL2 the PAS reset sequence is not available: Linux can authenticate a
+ *    firmware image (with qcom,needs-tzmem) but the remoteproc never leaves
+ *    reset, so qcom_q6v5_wait_for_start() always times out with -ETIMEDOUT.
+ *    "qcom,broken-reset" tells the remoteproc driver not to try starting them
+ *    at all and to attach to whichever of them the boot firmware left
+ *    running instead.  On probe the driver prints the SMP2P line state of all
+ *    four interrupts per DSP, which is what tells us whether attaching is
+ *    possible on this machine.
  *
  *  - pmic-glink needs the ADSP's rpmsg and LMH cannot set its thermal
  *    thresholds from EL2; both only produce errors there.
@@ -101,15 +104,18 @@ &apps_smmu {
 };
 
 &remoteproc_adsp {
-	status = "disabled";
+	qcom,broken-reset;
+	qcom,needs-tzmem;
 };
 
 &remoteproc_cdsp {
-	status = "disabled";
+	qcom,broken-reset;
+	qcom,needs-tzmem;
 };
 
 &remoteproc_slpi {
-	status = "disabled";
+	qcom,broken-reset;
+	qcom,needs-tzmem;
 };
 
 &{/pmic-glink} {
-- 
